NOTES = """# ACTF r04 — 2026-09-02-final-heavy (grok-4.6)

Quota Q=2 designed coding episodes (FACTORY_QUOTAS=2). IDs `{id_a}`, `{id_b}` (mill prefix `act`, unused in-repo). Envelope: id/goal/steps/outcome/reward/meta. Tools restricted to verify_execution KNOWN_TOOLS (`bash`/`read_file`/`edit_file`/`write_file`/`search`/`gh`/`kubectl`/`gate-cli`/`aws`/`jq`/`refuse`). meta.round=4 factory=agentic-coding-trajectory-factory generator=grok-4.6 run_label=2026-09-02-final-heavy sim_or_real=designed. meta.rights RM-793 research_only; training_ready false. Live-tree write is create-only (`{batch_name}`); never clobbered `batch-r01.jsonl` / `NOTES-r01.md` / r02 / r21 / r22 / r41 / r61 / r62 / r63 / r64 and never wrote 2026-08-17/2026-08-30. Distinct from window r01 (sanderling inclusive-after Rust pager / whimbrel Node inflight Map race), r02 (jacanasub re.sub count-vs-flags / tattlerbool argparse type=bool), r21 duration-json-ns / sqlite executescript, r22 sql NullString / SameSite morsel, r41 unpack-be-le / PVC RWO, r61 tzdata LoadLocation / tofu count-index, r62 parsedate -0000 / dunlincut unsorted dedup, r63 pem.Decode rest / tofu moved-block, r64 inet_aton abbrev / WaitForFirstConsumer. Addresses r02 NOTES gap (stale 502 fixture whose want disagrees with a second document) and leaves mill lots and Kubernetes YAML (r64 already returned k8s volumeBindingMode). Invented repos `git.bitternfen.internal/pkg/bitternid-harbor.git` and `git.avocetfen.internal/cli/avocetsv-harbor.git`. Linear RM-793 remains the rights tracker.

| id | codebase / harness | bug class | result | reward.total |
|----|--------------------|-----------|--------|--------------|
| {id_a} | Go 1.22 harbor event-id helper + event-ids fixtures / go test + aws s3api + jq | schema mismatch: `json.Unmarshal` into `any` stores id as float64 so 2^53+1 rounds; first fix string-only decoder rejected number payloads | success; TestParseMixedIDs; PR 241 | 0.58 |
| {id_b} | Python 3.12 dest-row splitter CLI / pytest + gate-cli | silent split: `str.split(',')` broke quoted dest names; first fix quote-lookahead regex still split doubled quotes | incomplete HIL/prod apply; AV-83; freeze AV-60 | 0.28 |

## Step counts, noise, plan change
- {id_a}: 15 steps. 429 at step 4 (`gh api` golang encoding/json decode.go, retry-after 5) -> recovery step 5 (`sleep 6` + read `docs/json-number-id.md`). 502 at step 6 (`aws s3api get-object` bitternfen-specs event-ids ELB) -> recovery step 7 (`jq` committed `fixtures/event-ids.json` against stale `fixtures/event-ids.stale.json`). Plan change at step 8: jq join shows want already 9007199254740993 while stale/got are 9007199254740992; abandon truncated-transit. Debug loop: 9 edit string-only id -> 10 write mixed-id go test -> 11 FAIL id not string -> 12 re-read parse.go -> 13 UseNumber patch -> 14 go test ok.
- {id_b}: 17 steps. 502 at step 4 (`aws s3api get-object` avocetfen-specs dest-rows ELB) -> recovery step 5 (`jq` committed `fixtures/dest-rows.json` against stale `fixtures/dest-rows.stale.json`, writes /tmp/avocetsv-traces.json). 429 at step 6 (`gh api` cpython csv.rst, retry-after 7) -> recovery step 7 (`sleep 8` + read `docs/csv-quoted.md`). Plan change at step 8: jq want already two fields while got is three on the quoted dest name; abandon remounting remote traces. Debug loop: 10 edit regex split -> 11 write escaped-quote pytest -> 12 FAIL got three fields -> 13 re-read split.py -> 14 csv.reader patch -> 15 4 passed. `refuse` at step 9 blocks deleting dest.lock. gate-cli REJECT at 16; AV-83 at 17.

## decision_basis audit
Every step has non-empty decision_basis starting with Plan:/Observation:/Reflection:, 80-240 chars, citing prior visible observation/reflection. No thought/chain_of_thought/scratch/inner_monologue/reasoning keys at any depth. Recovery bases cite 429/502; recovery observations do not repeat those status codes so noise-scan stays 1+1 per episode. Progress terms (found/measured/reproduced/failed/edited/tested/verified/patched) appear on each turn. Word "hypothesis" kept out of observations.

## Reward
Unweighted numeric sum; success is a label. Cost sits under reward.cost. json-float64-id: 0.40+0.12+0.08-0.02=0.58. csv-quoted-comma: 0.24+0.10+0.08-0.12-0.02=0.28.

## Realism / weak recovery
Good: `encoding/json` storing numbers in `any` as float64 is a real snowflake-id footgun; a string-only `id.(string)` decoder is the equally tempting OpenAPI-shaped wrong fix and the mixed-id test names the contract (number 9007199254740993 plus string `"9007199254740993"` plus small 1001). `str.split(',')` breaking `"harbor, quay"` is the usual dest-CSV trap; a quote-lookahead regex still cannot satisfy a test that requires doubled quotes `"harbor, ""quay"""`. Stale 502 fallback now compares dest want exact 9007199254740993 / two fields against a second file still on the rounded id / three-token split (r02 densification). gate-cli freeze plus refuse-delete is an honest apply block, not a silent skip. Weak: the Go measure step still shells a python float print as a stand-in before go test; regex failure mode is one doubled-quote row rather than a nested quotes+newline CSV. Next densification: a reviewer asking to keep string-only decode "so partner B string clients never see json.Number", or a 502 whose local dest-rows fixture is rewritten after the csv.reader patch and still lists three fields.

Novel coverage: 47%
"""


def create_only(path: str, data: str) -> None:
    flags = os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL | os.O_WRONLY
    fd = os.open(path, flags, 0o644)
    with os.fdopen(fd, "w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
        fh.write(data)
        if not data.endswith("\n"):
            fh.write("\n")


def pick_paths():
    batch = os.path.join(LIVE, "batch-r04.jsonl")
    notes = os.path.join(LIVE, "NOTES-r04.md")
    if not os.path.exists(batch) and not os.path.exists(notes):
        return batch, notes, "batch-r04.jsonl", "NOTES-r04.md"
    batch_c = os.path.join(LIVE, "batch-r04c.jsonl")
    notes_c = os.path.join(LIVE, "NOTES-r04c.md")
    if not os.path.exists(batch_c) and not os.path.exists(notes_c):
        return batch_c, notes_c, "batch-r04c.jsonl", "NOTES-r04c.md"
    raise SystemExit("both r04 and r04c already exist; refusing overwrite")


def main() -> None:
    live_ids = census_live_ids()
    slug_a = "json-float64-id-bitternid"
    slug_b = "csv-quoted-comma-avocetsv"
    id_a = f"act-r04-{slug_a}-{hid(slug_a)}"
    id_b = f"act-r04-{slug_b}-{hid(slug_b)}"
    if id_a in live_ids or id_b in live_ids:
        raise SystemExit(f"id collision {id_a} {id_b}")
    plants = "bitternfen avocetfen bitternid avocetsv"
    blob = " ".join(live_ids).lower()
    for tok in plants.split():
        if tok in blob:
            raise SystemExit(f"plant token collision {tok}")
    ep_a = episode_a(id_a)
    ep_b = episode_b(id_b)
    validate(ep_a)
    validate(ep_b)
    batch_path, notes_path, batch_name, notes_name = pick_paths()
    body = (
        json.dumps(ep_a, ensure_ascii=False, separators=(",", ":"))
        + "\n"
        + json.dumps(ep_b, ensure_ascii=False, separators=(",", ":"))
        + "\n"
    )
    notes = NOTES.format(id_a=id_a, id_b=id_b, batch_name=batch_name)
    create_only(batch_path, body)
    try:
        create_only(notes_path, notes)
    except FileExistsError:
        os.remove(batch_path)
        raise
    print(json.dumps({
        "batch": batch_path,
        "notes": notes_path,
        "ids": [id_a, id_b],
        "steps": [len(ep_a["steps"]), len(ep_b["steps"])],
        "batch_name": batch_name,
        "notes_name": notes_name,
    }))


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
